From 7bdf7e647b6b87913c7e3e1a476ac9e737c741a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:19:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): integrate public containment and certified
 replica fences [daveey]

Ordinary triage is dispatchable and generic lifecycle writes can release consumers, so non-human containment needs independent durable stop custody, admitted actor identity and authenticated release evidence. Share CLI/tool service, register connection guards, exclude held work from maintenance, and project certified canonical rows without trusting the sync-applying flag. Preserve edges and independent spend holds. Commit exact requests before I/O; retain provisional holds after unknown delivery and permit original-byte recovery by the live nominated authority.

Proof: canonical runner 21 files, 422 tests passed, 0 failed; scripts/check --base origin/main passes. Includes real SQLite page application/reopen and CLI/tool adapter paths, with Hub transport doubles explicitly not live Board proofs. Consumer run exposed legacy no-UID trigger incompatibility; conditional trigger definitions restore ordinary local event writes without weakening protected history. Full guard mutation inventory, real cross-process Board transport, independent final Opus/core review, exact-head CI and landing/deployment remain mandatory. No live relay or retention mutations; implementation remains incomplete.
